+# MarufYT Phase 4.1 — final IPA security audit
+
+Date: 2026-11-03, Asia/Kuala_Lumpur. Developer: arifular1f.
+Repository source reviewed: `657aed1`, branch `phase4.1-performance-ui`;
+compiled implementation: `1bd5c82221fb494ccb7aab75345c6875eb2a9917`.
+Phase 4 baseline: source `c044eb4`, package `1.1.4+marufyt.6`.
+Target supplied by user: iPhone 15 Pro Max, iOS 27.2; no device connected.
+
+## 1. Executive summary
+
+Both existing `1.1.4+marufyt.7` ROOTLESS IPAs were inspected in place, including
+their native binaries, XML entitlements, Info.plist, resources and credential-pattern
+candidates. Source network/storage/authentication paths and the complete Phase 4.1
+source diff were reviewed. No app code, settings, workflow or build was changed.
+
+**No Critical or High vulnerability was confirmed in this static scope. Findings
+were identified:** unfiltered playback request material is persisted in a
+Files-visible directory (Medium); credential-capable SABR requests lack an explicit
+destination boundary across application-level redirects (Medium hardening weakness);
+some media requests still accept HTTP (Low); and diagnostics retain viewing data
+with incomplete generic redaction (Low). All four issues are inherited from Phase 4,
+not introduced by the `.7` changes. Actual stolen tokens, an exploited redirect or
+an observed cleartext transfer were **not** demonstrated.
+
+The prior statement that authentication material is never stored is too broad:
+the code indiscriminately serializes native headers/body; what credentials are
+actually present in those objects needs controlled device testing. No credentials
+or matching API-key values are reproduced in this report or evidence files.
+
+Static regression checks found **no new permissions, imports, linked libraries,
+literal URL hosts, executable files or host tracking components** versus `.6`.
+This is not proof of runtime safety, exhaustive endpoint discovery or absence of
+malware in proprietary/third-party code. No automatic fixes were made because no
+confirmed Critical issue was found, consistent with the audit-only instruction.
+
