+## 3. Permissions, entitlements and privacy manifests
+
+Both host Info.plists contain these usage descriptions, byte-unchanged from `.6`:
+`NSContactsUsageDescription`, `NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription`,
+`NSCameraUsageDescription`, `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription`,
+`NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription`, `NSAppleMusicUsageDescription`,
+`NSBluetoothPeripheralUsageDescription`, `NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription`,
+`NSUserTrackingUsageDescription`. These declarations permit permission requests;
+they do not prove a grant, collection or transmission occurred.
+
+`UIFileSharingEnabled` and `LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace` are true.
+`UIBackgroundModes` includes `audio`, `remote-notification`, `fetch`,
+`external-accessory`. They are identical in both builds and to Phase 4.
+
+The host's embedded XML entitlement metadata includes Google application identity,
+three Google keychain groups, three application groups, production APNs,
+associated domains/webcredentials, multicast, Wi-Fi info, user-assigned device name,
+Siri, group sessions, notification communication/time-sensitive, declared-age-range,
+StoreKit request data and alternate video decoder selection. No broad Keychain or
+filesystem entitlement was added by MarufYT. The tweak has no XML entitlement blob
+of its own; it executes with its host process's effective privileges.
+
+**Signing limitation:** these are signing-required IPAs. Retained Code Signature
+load commands/embedded entitlement blobs are not validated effective entitlements.
+DER entitlement blobs were detected but not decoded independently. No Apple
+signature-chain, provisioning or installation validation was possible on Windows.
+No embedded provisioning profile was found. Re-signing can change identity, groups,
+push capability and SSO behavior; it requires a fresh signed-artifact/device review.
+
+No `PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` file was found in either archive (or either Phase 4 IPA).
+That absence is a transparency/distribution review item (Informational), not evidence
+that no personal data or required-reason APIs are used, nor a legal compliance verdict.
+
+**Photos declaration review item (Informational):** the dedicated
+`NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription` key is absent, while
+`DownloadCoordinator.mm:295` and `PostImageSaver.mm:53` request add-only access.
+The host's broader photo-library description is present. Fresh-permission handling,
+prompt/denial/termination behavior and whether that declaration is sufficient on the
+target OS were not tested; no crash is asserted from static evidence alone.
+
+## 4. Device-access capabilities
+
+Capabilities are shared within a process; a dylib is not a separate permission sandbox.
+The observations below describe reviewed calls, not a claim that an injected library
+could never use other host-granted APIs or that jailbroken-device isolation is intact.
+
+| Capability | MarufYT evidence and actual access boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| Contacts | No direct contact-store API call found in `Tweak/`; host declares contact access and explicitly describes sending contacts to YouTube. Grant/use/transmission NOT TESTED |
+| Photos/media library | Actual saving paths: `DownloadCoordinator.mm:267–298`, `PostImageSaver.mm:23–56`, `ProfilePictureViewer.mm:345`, `YTKACEDownloadsController.mm:1601`; Photos framework/imports confirm capability, not that a permission was granted. Host can also request broader photo/music access |
+| Camera | Host purpose string/API surface; no capture-device/session use found in tweak source. Actual host camera use NOT TESTED |
+| Microphone | Host purpose string; tweak uses playback audio sessions (`PiPControls.mm:282`, download player) and reads output volume, not a reviewed recording path. AVFoundation presence alone does not prove recording |
+| GPS/location | Host location declaration; no direct CLLocationManager use found in tweak. IP geolocation remains possible for every contacted service |
+| Clipboard | Explicit copy actions write to general pasteboard: `CopyCommentHooks.mm:222`, `TranscriptExport.mm:572`, `PostImageSaver.mm:281`, `DownloadCoordinator.mm:792/803`, diagnostics viewer `YTKACERootOptionsController.mm:198`. No continuous clipboard-reading path identified; host capabilities remain separate |
+| Files/documents | Actual sandbox reads/writes, media import/export, backup/restore, Files-visible downloads and request seeds. User-selected document URLs may grant additional scoped access. No unrestricted device filesystem access demonstrated |
+| Device metadata | `SABRDownloader.mm:520–541` constructs actual device model/OS, locale/region, screen size/scale and timezone fields for media requests. These are fingerprinting attributes, not a unique hardware identifier. Other clients use constant model/OS identities. No direct IDFA/IDFV/UDID collector found in tweak |
+| Keychain/credentials | Dummy-item access-group discovery and host SSO access-group hooks; host authorizer token access for playlist requests. See section 8. No device-wide Keychain dump found |
+| Notifications | Host APNs metadata/background mode and notification extensions; tweak NSNotificationCenter observers are local process events, not proof of push registration. Signing/user permission determine effective notification access |
+| Background activity | Actual network/media work and timers can outlive a screen; audio/PiP and download callbacks remain. No new background-session daemon/updater found. Actual suspension, fetch/push and background traffic NOT TESTED |
