+## 6. Integration defaults and Private Lookup review
+
+Fresh-default source behavior, **not** a read of the user's installed preferences:
+
+| Integration | Fresh default | Background/automatic behavior after opt-in |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| SponsorBlock | OFF: no true default for its Enabled key; bool lookup yields false | Automatic lookup per relevant video without another tap |
+| Private Lookup | OFF, separately opt-in | Changes lookup route only; votes/submissions and DeArrow still expose full context |
+| DeArrow titles / thumbnail replacement | OFF / mode 0 | Visible feed content can cause branding/thumbnail requests |
+| AiSList hiding filters | OFF (both preference flags absent/false) | List refresh on activation/staleness; does not send the watched ID in list-download requests |
+| AiSList reporting | Explicit user action and confirmation | Channel metadata lookup may precede submission confirmation; submission sends handle/link/name |
+| Playback/download helpers | Individual settings/user activity control paths; background audio default ON, download button default OFF | Native request capture/restoration hooks are installed independently of the download-button toggle |
+
+Evidence: `Preferences.mm:43–150,280–286`, `SponsorHooks.mm:41–44`,
+`SponsorPreferences.mm:53–76`, `SponsorClient.mm:12,72`, `DeArrow.mm:51–75`,
+`ContentVisibilityHooks.mm:1119–1121`, `Entry.mm:15–41`. Restored/imported settings
+override fresh defaults. No claim that the user's current integrations are disabled.
+
+Private Lookup validates an 11-character allowed-character video ID, performs one
+SHA-256 round, and sends the first four lowercase hex characters (16 bits) in the
+path plus category JSON. Invalid IDs return before sending; no full-ID fallback.
+The response must be an array; the exact case-sensitive matching video ID is
+selected locally. Segment category, numeric/finite/ordered times and action checks
+are retained; unexpected entries are ignored. A 1 MiB check occurs **after** a data
+task accumulates the response, so it is not a streaming download-size cap.
+Private Lookup reduces request specificity; it does not anonymize IP/timing,
+related requests or this enumerable video-ID space. No additional live API requests
+were sent for this audit. Objective-C response parsing and service behavior remain
+untested on the target device.
+
+## 7. Binary, dependency and executable review
+
+`MarufYT.dylib` imports 23 system framework/library dependencies besides its own
+install name: Objective-C, Foundation/CoreFoundation/UIKit, JavaScriptCore,
+AVFoundation/AVKit/AVFAudio/AudioToolbox, Photos, QuartzCore, MediaPlayer, Security,
+SystemConfiguration, UniformTypeIdentifiers, VideoToolbox, CoreMedia/CoreVideo,
+CoreGraphics/ImageIO, zlib, libc++ and libSystem. All dependency install names are
+system paths; no newly linked external dylib or missing new dependency was found.
+The full import/load/rpath inventory covers every native component in the JSON files.
+
+No `system`, `popen`, `posix_spawn[p]`, `execve/execv/execl`, `fork`, `dlopen` or
+`ptrace` import was found in the tweak's undefined-symbol table, and no corresponding
+source execution path was identified. File APIs (`open`, `unlink`, NSFileManager),
+environment access, ObjC message dispatch/method replacement and JavaScriptCore
+are present and expected. This is an import/source check, not proof against
+obfuscated, indirect or host-mediated execution.
+
+`dladdr` and `dlsym` **are** imported. The former has source uses in `UI/Assets.mm:9`,
+`Features/Streaming/StreamingHooks.mm:203` and `Features/Interface/MiscellaneousHooks.mm:115`
+for image/address inspection. The latter is present in the existing
+`Vendor/FFmpeg/lib/libavcodec.a` member `videotoolboxenc.o`; the preserved FFmpeg
+8.1.2 source `libavcodec/videotoolboxenc.c:146,157` resolves VideoToolbox symbols
+with it. See DYNAMIC_SYMBOL_REVIEW.txt. Absence of `dlopen` must not be restated as
+absence of all runtime symbol lookup.
+
+Runtime code processing **does exist**: `ChallengeSolver.mm:20–77` loads bundled
+minified solver libraries and player-derived/preprocessed script into JavaScriptCore,
+with cache files and error handling. It is not shell execution. The minified solver
+and statically linked FFmpeg are third-party attack surfaces; no full code audit,
+CVE sweep, sanitizer/fuzzer run or exploitability assessment was performed. Build
+configuration (`Scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh:81–90`) disables FFmpeg networking and
+enables the local file protocol; application networking still uses Foundation.
+
+Widevine is an opaque existing Google DRM component, and Latest additionally has
+the original Swift compatibility binary/extensions. No new unexplained native
+executable or executable script was added by `.7`. JavaScript wrappers and
+`gRPCCertificates.bundle/roots.pem` are existing host resources; the two solver JS
+files are existing tweak resources. The PEM resource contains trust certificates,
+not a signing credential. No P12/PFX/private signing key/profile was found in the
+reviewed package paths. Opaque dependencies are not certified safe by this finding.
+
+Credential-pattern scan: Latest has 18 Google API-key-pattern candidates and one
+private-key marker candidate; Stable has 16 and one. Every candidate's path, offset
+and SHA256 fingerprint is identical to its Phase 4 counterpart. Google-client API
+keys in a shipped app are not automatically private server secrets; restrictions
+and abuse potential were not validated. The private-key marker in YouTube has no
+complete PEM key at the matching location. No confirmed new credential exposure
+was established; only categories/fingerprints, never values, are saved. Binary-only
+or encrypted/assembled secrets can escape these patterns.
+
+## 8. Authentication, storage and deletion
+
+The host's executable sections and Google SSO URL schemes are retained, but
+**the tweak does intentionally hook SSO compatibility**, not merely leave all
+authentication behavior untouched. `SideloadCompatibility.mm:27–60,261–330` probes
+attributes of a dummy generic-password item to discover its allowed access group,
+maps SSO keychain-group methods to that group, adjusts Safari-sign-in configuration,
+handles URL-delegate routing and supplies application-group fallback locations.
+It also reports App Store environment flags through Google utilities. Those hooks
+are unchanged from Phase 4. They do not grant arbitrary Keychain groups or prove
+Google login/account switching works after signing.
+
+`PlaylistDownloader.mm:572–659` obtains an access token from the host authorizer
+or an authorized probe request and attaches it to a hard-coded Google browse
+request, with an ephemeral cookie-disabled session. No explicit Google-password
+collector or Google-token addition to SponsorBlock/DeArrow/AiSList requests was
+identified. Redirect credential stripping, native cookie state and token lifetime
+are NOT TESTED; SABR raw-header replay/persistence are separate concerns below.
+
+Storage reviewed:
+
+- Settings, DeArrow branding/video IDs, visitor IDs and a random persistent
+  SponsorBlock contributor ID reside in ordinary sandbox preferences/caches.
+  They are not a Keychain token vault. The new artwork cache is bounded and in memory.
+- `YTKACEApplicationSupportDirectory()` actually returns `Documents/YTKACE`;
+  media and request seeds share this Files-visible tree. F-01 documents the impact.
+- `DownloadLog.mm:7–51,98–150` separately places diagnostics in real Application
+  Support (Caches/temp fallback), requests backup exclusion and
+  CompleteUntilFirstUserAuthentication protection, and limits/trims the log.
+  These calls' success and fallback behavior are not device-verified.
+- `SABRDownloader.mm:886–890` writes a raw outgoing protobuf diagnostic to temp
+  independently of the debug-log toggle. Scratch purge (`:717–752`) can remove
+  `ytkace-*.pb` dumps; it is not assured immediate secure deletion.
+- Clear Cache (`YTKACESettingsPages.mm:1935–1952`) removes a Cache subdirectory,
+  download scratch and system caches, not all request seeds at the root.
+  A stale restored player seed has a deletion path (`DownloadHooks.mm:865–877`),
+  but no comprehensive account-sign-out/session-change purge was identified for
+  both persisted seed types. Host token revocation must be checked separately.
+- Explicit backups filter settings to `YTKACE.Preference.*` and enumerate the
+  Downloads subdirectory (`YTKACEBackupManager.mm:96–120,363–391`), not arbitrary
+  Keychain contents/root seeds. Restore normalizes/restricts archive paths, stored
+  entry format and CRC (`:479–520`). This is source evidence, not fuzzing or proof
+  of safe handling of every malformed/oversized backup. Ordinary device/iCloud
+  backup of Documents and exclusion/protection of seeds remain unverified.
+
+## 9. Findings and severity
+
+Severity denotes the reviewed weakness/impact, not proof that an attack occurred.
+All following source paths are relative to `Tweak/` unless otherwise noted.
+
+### F-01 — Medium: unfiltered request material in Files-visible persistent storage
+
+**Confirmed:** `Runtime/Preferences.mm:403–449` returns Documents/YTKACE despite
+its helper name. `Features/Downloads/SABRDownloader.mm:36–64,136–155` serializes
+native request body and all headers without a sensitive-header filter to
+`sabr-seed.plist`. `DownloadHooks.mm:368–379,541–551,833–849` serializes the native
+player request to `player-request.pb`. `Tools/marufyt_package.py:197–198` enables
+Files sharing. Entry.mm restores seeds on startup. These capture paths do not
+require clicking Download and are not gated by the debug-log toggle.
+
+**Impact:** anyone/app given access to this Documents tree or a copied device backup
+can obtain session-bearing request material if those runtime objects contain it;
+there is also viewing/account-context retention. No secret values were extracted
+from a phone, so the presence of a live Authorization/Cookie token is conditional,
+not claimed proven. Root seeds lack explicit expiry/sign-out purge and dedicated
+backup exclusion/protection at these write sites. Same issue exists in Phase 4.
+
+**Minimal recommendation, not applied:** stop persisting credential-bearing headers
+and opaque authenticated request bodies; rebuild ephemeral state when needed. If a
+nonsecret seed is essential, use an explicit field allowlist, actual private
+Application Support, requested file protection/backup exclusion, bounded expiry
+and sign-out purge, with migration/deletion of old seeds. Keep media in Documents.
+Review/suppress the unconditional raw outgoing protobuf dump as part of this change.
+
+### F-02 — Medium: no explicit destination boundary for native-header SABR replay
+
+**Confirmed control gap:** `Features/Downloads/SABRDownloader.mm:1013–1049`
+accepts `self.serverURL` and copies native headers except six content/host headers;
+Authorization/Cookie are not excluded. `:1476–1482` accepts a protobuf redirect
+string into that URL without scheme/host validation. The next request is built
+with headers again. This is an application-level redirect, so Foundation stripping
+Authorization on an ordinary cross-origin HTTP redirect does not resolve it.
+
+**Impact conditions:** a malicious/compromised stream response or otherwise
+attacker-controlled serverURL could direct available session headers/body to an
+unintended destination. No attacker control, populated credential header, or actual
+exfiltration was demonstrated. HTTPS/system TLS still protects normal trusted
+responses. This is an inherited missing trust boundary, not evidence of a backdoor.
+
+**Minimal recommendation, not applied:** validate initial and redirected media
+destinations against the verified scheme/origin policy; explicitly restrict header
+replay to the appropriate trusted origin and exclude authentication cookies/tokens
+elsewhere. Validate custom protobuf redirects as well as Foundation redirects.
+
+### F-03 — Low: HTTPS enforcement is incomplete for generic media requests
+
+**Confirmed:** `Features/Downloads/StreamResolver.mm:155–164` accepts a scheme
+starting with `http`, including HTTP; `DownloadCoordinator.mm:2220–2224` creates a
+download task from its URL without an explicit HTTPS check. SABR URL handling has
+the gap in F-02. In contrast, the Phase 4 avatar/post/caption guard remains intact.
+The host's four inherited ATS HTTP exceptions mean ATS is not a universal
+HTTPS-only policy. No observed HTTP transfer or general ATS bypass is claimed.
+
+**Recommendation, not applied:** require HTTPS and a valid host on all remote fetch
+paths and redirects, while distinguishing legitimate local-file operations.
+
+### F-04 — Low: diagnostics retain viewing context and redact only selected formats
+
+**Confirmed:** `Features/Downloads/DownloadLog.mm:78–86` writes regular diagnostic
+messages regardless of the DebugLogs preference; only `YTKACEDebugLog` is opt-in.
+Call sites include video IDs, paths, request sizes and errors (for example
+`DownloadHooks.mm:1348–1349,1396` and `SABRDownloader.mm:889`). Regexes at
+`:98–119` cover bearer strings, URL queries and selected key=value fields, not
+arbitrary JSON or Cookie header formats. The existing synthetic Python approximation
+removes three covered fixtures and leaves two uncovered fixtures, as expected.
+
+**Impact/limits:** local viewing/diagnostic information persists until cleared or
+trimmed; arbitrary future/raw error payloads are not guaranteed secret-free. No
+real token in a log was observed. Location/protection is better than Documents,
+and no log-upload path was found. This is not a remote exfiltration finding.
+**Recommendation, not applied:** minimize routine per-video logs and use structured
+allowlisted fields; never pass raw credentials, headers, bodies or server responses
+to a generic regex redactor. Verify native ICU/Foundation behavior before claiming
+redaction guarantees.
+
+### Informational observations and remaining review items
+
+- **I-01:** full video IDs go to opted-in normal SponsorBlock/DeArrow; Private Lookup
+  protects lookup route only. This is documented service behavior, not a newly found
+  vulnerability. Defaults and disclosures are in sections 5–6.
+- **I-02:** host permissions, tracking-related literals, broad capability surface,
+  ATS exceptions, missing privacy manifests and signing-dependent entitlements are
+  inherited; none should be mistaken for zero-permission/zero-tracking operation.
+- **I-03:** add-only Photos declaration needs target-OS validation (section 3).
+- **I-04:** `YTKACEMediaImporter.mm:98,110` has unbounded muxer/artwork completion
+  waits on worker paths. The prior Low availability concern remains; no remote
+  denial-of-service exploit demonstrated. No sanitizer/fuzz result is available.
+- **I-05:** whole-host Google API-key patterns and a non-complete private-key marker
+  are baseline candidates, not confirmed leaked private credentials (section 7).
